# What gui/solve_cli answers on each sketch here (tools/regress.sh): the
# name, a time limit in seconds, then the answer's ok, red, pins and cls
# lines joined by "; " (the box and the reasons are not compared; a drop's
# and a conflict's nd are, in cls). A .raw name is the sketch with the
# repeats left out of its plain input (the page sent that before S8; it
# sends every constraint now). Since sk-13a's switch (PLAN-sk13a S5) the
# repeats are amber and the raw sketches certify like the others. Since
# sk-13b's switch so does vertical-twice: the repeated vertical's equation
# is dropped by directions, where segments 31, 24, 23 and 4 have nonzero
# length, so it is amber (two positions on in the raw sketch), where sk-13a
# refused it as Over. From hchain to cancel are PLAN-sk13a S8's small
# sketches (s8.mjs); angle-lines is Danielle's slowsketches sketch(5),
# refused (honestly: as drawn, its angle's side condition fails) after
# every precision. From right-angles on are PLAN-sk13b B8's (b8.mjs; the
# audit's sketches A, B and V last). Two of them are red and not
# certified: in h-par-v the page's drawing keeps the red Vertical (a merge,
# so the drawing has it), and the Parallel cannot be solved for with the
# pins chosen; in audit-v the relaxation pulls toward the red VDistance.
# par-collapse stays refused (PLAN-sk13b decision 4).
